# Git push policy

- Push to your own named branch (`chat3/*` etc.) without asking; never push to `main`, never force-push.
- The agent may stage and commit when the user explicitly asks to commit.
- After a commit, push to your own named branch. The canonical git rule is in `docs/roles/README.md`.
- Do not assume permission to push to `main`; provide the commands and wait for the user.
- Prefer: show `git status` / branch tracking context, then the precise `git push` (or `git push -u origin HEAD`) line for the user to copy.
- Work-state / what to prioritize next still comes from `docs/EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md` (see `execution-backlog.mdc`); push policy only covers publishing mechanics.
